  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital each day. During the outbreak, the hospital's weekly patient-admission report is reviewed by the hospital's administrative office. The report categorizes admitted patients by department, such as emergency medicine, pediatrics, and surgery. The hospital uses an electronic registration system to record each patient's admission date.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital ea...\n- {\"content\":\"The hospital admits **55 patients per day**.\\n\\nSince one week has **7 days**:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n55 \\\\times 7 = 385\\n\\\\]\\n\\nTherefore, the hospital can admit\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{385\\\\text{ patients per week}}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 50 patients are admitted into the hospital each day.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits **50 patients per day**. Since there are **7 days in a week**:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the hospital can admit:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{350\\text{ patients per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many beds does the hospital need to handle its daily admissions for one week? Additionally, here are some details: the hospital's admissions office is open seven days during the week. Each daily admission requires one completed intake form before the patient is assigned to a bed.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits **50 patients per day**. Since each patient requires one bed:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 1 = 50\n\\]\n\nThus, the hospital needs at least\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{50\\text{ beds}}\n\\]\n\nto accommodate the daily admissions, assuming each patient occupies a bed for one day. Over the full week, this represents \\(50 \\times 7 = 350\\) patient-bed placements.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the hospital has a capacity of 1050 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350 \\text{ patients per week}\n\\]\n\nWith a capacity of **1,050 beds**, it has enough capacity to handle these admissions. Comparing the weekly admissions with total capacity:\n\n\\[\n1050 - 350 = 700\n\\]\n\nSo, the hospital has **700 beds more than the number of patients admitted in one week**. Assuming each patient needs a bed for only one day, **50 beds are needed at any given time**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now can you extend that? Specifically: How many unoccupied beds are in the hospital after 2 weeks? One more thing you should know: One-fifth of the hospital beds are occupied.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital has:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1050=210\n\\]\n\noccupied beds initially, so it starts with:\n\n\\[\n1050-210=840\n\\]\n\nunoccupied beds.\n\nOver two weeks, the hospital admits:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\n\\]\n\npatients. Assuming these patients remain in the hospital and no patients are discharged, the number of unoccupied beds afterward is:\n\n\\[\n840-700=140\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{140\\text{ unoccupied beds}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — The time period is 2 weeks.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The time period is already **2 weeks**, so the calculation remains:\n\n1. Initially occupied beds:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1050=210\n\\]\n\n2. Initially unoccupied beds:\n\n\\[\n1050-210=840\n\\]\n\n3. Admissions over 2 weeks:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\n\\]\n\n4. Unoccupied beds afterward:\n\n\\[\n840-700=\\boxed{140}\n\\]\n\nThus, assuming no patients are discharged during the two weeks, **140 beds remain unoccupied**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. The hospital has a capacity of 1000 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With a capacity of **1,000 beds**:\n\n1. Initially occupied beds:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1000=200\n\\]\n\n2. Initially unoccupied beds:\n\n\\[\n1000-200=800\n\\]\n\n3. Admissions over 2 weeks:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\n\\]\n\n4. Remaining unoccupied beds:\n\n\\[\n800-700=\\boxed{100\\text{ beds}}\n\\]\n\nAssuming no patients are discharged, **100 beds remain unoccupied after 2 weeks**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
